# Buyback Monitor Skill

When the user asks for A-share share-buyback monitoring, repurchase scans, buyback progress, cancellation buybacks, buyback intensity, buyback purpose classification, buyback price bands, or a buyback watch report, use the local skill package.

Preferred local project path:

```text
.cursor/skills/buyback-monitor
```

Workflow:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/buyback-monitor/SKILL.md`.
2. For routing, stage/purpose/intensity definitions, dedup rules, report format, empty-data handling, or QA, also read `.cursor/skills/buyback-monitor/references/buyback-playbook.md`.
3. Validate generated reports with `.cursor/skills/buyback-monitor/scripts/validate_report.py`.
4. Use the local `pandadata-api` skill for the exact `get_repurchase` contract before any real API call.
5. Deduplicate events across procedure stages before counting; report the latest stage; always distinguish 预案 (planned range) from executed amounts.
6. Classify purpose from source signals verbatim (assert 注销 only with `write_off_date` or explicit cancellation purpose); label ambiguous cases 未分类.
7. Preserve source method names, query windows, announcement dates, stages, and missing-data notes. Do not invent amounts, ratios, stages, purposes, credentials, or investment advice.
